  "implemented": [
    "Public notification/permission payloads are exact finite DTOs; they carry no app/action/icon/URL/path or caller-selected policy. Current physical main document and captured engine gate native ingress and final delivery.",
    "Permission get can participate in hydration through an already-captured document; permission request and display remain fenced until hydration. Replacement document checks reject retired results without replay.",
    "The Source launch capability selects the actual AgentManager native notification host. Private general/status operations remain outside the public command map. Actual manager transition detection emits status requests; native derives inactive-only policy from that operation and checks real main focus.",
    "Bounded SQL reads title-prefix bytes and parent completion scalars without full task or credential/large JSON getters. Exact valid short text, fallback and completed-parent suppression persist; malformed UTF8/control text is normalized and clipped output is marked.",
    "Optional native refusal, malformed reply, deadline or absence do not disconnect the durable service or retry an uncertain notification. Raw callbacks remain retained by actual owner cleanup; transport disconnection still performs its normal teardown.",
    "Linux async GIO obtains the session connection and exact unique notification server. Requests target only that server; raw variant byte bounds precede Rust server/action string copies. Fixed application/action/hints and escaped text grant no content-driven action dispatcher.",
    "Native owns bounded notification IDs and two signal subscriptions. Fixed clicks require original engine epoch, exact connection/server/owned ID and trusted current main window, then reopen/focus the app. Generic notifications remain unconditional; status notifications refuse while main is focused.",
    "Accepted IDs are recorded before late caller checks. Public timeout/drop revokes future effects without releasing real GIO callback captures. Independent cleanup works after normal work admission closes, joins actual replies/subscription retirement and closes only captured-server owned IDs.",
    "Only structured InvalidId/NameHasNoOwner/ServiceUnknown absence acknowledges retirement; other cleanup failures retain ownership for explicit retry. A changed daemon is unavailable rather than a redirect of old authority."
  ],
